    "result_text": "Done. The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 reworked customer-code generation:\n- Renamed the call site to `nextCustomerCode(owner.getCity(), owner.getLastName())`.\n- Rewrote `nextCustomerCode` to build the new `'<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>'` format:\n  - `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the city\n  - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n  - `NNNN` = a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence, one more than the owners already in that city (previously it was a global sequence over all owners).\n- Extracted a small `prefix3(...)` helper since the CITY3 and LAST3 derivations are identical, and updated the Javadoc.\n\n## Values built from customerCode\n\nThe **membership number** is derived from `customerCode` in `OwnerMapper` (`owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + ...`), so it automatically rebuilds on the new format \u2014 no change needed there. That's the only value built on top of the customer code.\n\n## Verification\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests pass. The new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` shape) is green.",
